{
  "description": "std-site-header — the sticky top bar of a public website: brand (logo + name), navigation links with the current page marked (a link with children opens a dropdown), an optional language picker (std-language-picker: the same page in each language, default language at the root and the others under /<code>/), and an optional call-to-action button. On small screens the links fold into a menu opened by a toggle, with child links indented under their parent and the call-to-action button at the bottom. Links follow `href` (in-app path, #anchor, or absolute URL); the header action and the small-screen menu links also emit NAV_CLICKED { href, label }. Pick for marketing sites, docs portals and product websites; for signed-in app chrome use std-app-layout.",
  "ledger": {
    "entries": {
      "ent_01M3B9EHRNR3JQPJSD36PH5QV8": {
        "bakedName": "SiteHeaderView",
        "curName": "SiteHeaderView",
